{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Operator decision (2026-11-18): option (1)\n\nAdd a top-level `rebar --version` that prints `rebar <version> (<commit>)` from importlib.metadata and rebar._build_info.COMMIT, with probes in scripts/probe_rebar.py and the release wheel_test job. The operator explicitly approves this new CLI flag as an exception to the bug-fix no-new-flags rule. It is a standard CLI convention, and the release checklists already reference it. Options (2), a `rebar version` subcommand, and (3), wontfix, are rejected."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795051090799808198,"uuid":"0e5e66fe-4bca-4a26-8d67-f36250172e50"}